│ ☆  parity-bot  dotfiles     █  Agreed, and I think the README should say so explicitly. Here's what I'd add under Keys:        █                             │
│ ☆  parity-bot  hello-world  █                                                                                                  █                             │
│ ☆  parity-bot  lazy-demo    █  • j / k move one line and stop at either end of the file; they never wrap around.               █                             │
│                             █  • G jumps to the last line and g to the first.                                                  █                             │
│                             █  • J / K move by hunk, and stop at the first and the last hunk.                                  █                             │
│                             █                                                                                                  █                             │
│                             █  I also checked the three cases you listed against the current build. All three behave as        █                             │
│                             █  described, so I don't think we need a code change here, just the docs. If you want, I can       █                             │
│                             █  open a follow-up for the wrap-around idea, since a few people asked for it in the               █                             │
└─────────────────────────────█  discussion, but I'd keep it behind a setting so the default stays the same as today.            █                             │
┌─ [2] Pull Requests ─────────█                                                                                                  █he defaults when it is empty,│
│ #  Status  Author      Title█  One more thing: the help panel lists j as "Line down" but the footer says "Down". We should     █lse changes for people who   │
│ 8  open    parity-bot  A pul█  pick one. I'd go with the help panel's wording because it's more specific, and the footer       █                             │
│                             █  has room for it at 100 columns.                                                                 █                             │
│                             █                                                                                                  █                             │
│                             █  Steps I ran:                                                                                    █                             │
│                             █                                                                                                  █                             │
│                             █   1. Open a file longer than the screen                                                          █                             │
│                             █   2. Press G                                                                                     █                             │
│                             █   3. Press j, then k, then g                                                                     █                             │
│                             █   4. Press J and K on a file with three hunks                                                    █                             │
│                             █                                                                                                  █                             │
│                             █  Every one of them stopped where the docs will say it stops. The only surprise was K on the      █                             │
└─────────────────────────────█  first hunk, which does nothing rather than wrapping to the last one, and that matches the       █                             │
┌─ [3] Issues ────────────────█  rest.                                                                                           █                             │
